{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1794443364,"nonce":"0ALcl5m2qERizY+/baR9i2j8jTw=","target":"40fc6707f9aead81d7eba83efde1ec3e39923594dfe8dda535ee08ea85f9fa0c","message":"Rotating a motion container turns its box but not its label, and never its shadow\n\nFound by the animation-path harness (crates/blinc_recorder/tests/animation_paths.rs; BLINC_ANIM_PATHS_OUT=\u003cdir\u003e writes a contact sheet for each scene). A card with a text label sits in a motion container whose parent is the card's size, so the pivot is the card's centre.\n\nMeasured on a plain card (no border, no shadow, so the only white pixels are the label), the principal axis of the label's pixels after the card has turned:\n- rotate only, card turned 35 deg: label 2.7 deg\n- rotate and scale, 35 deg: label 2.1 deg\n- rotate and fade, 35 deg: label 1.0 deg\n- nested, outer translate over inner scale and rotate, 20 deg: label 2.1 deg\n- nested, inner rotate only, 20 deg: label 2.7 deg\nThe label is level in every case. (An earlier version of this note said the label turned in the nested scene; that was an eyeball error.) A CSS keyframe or transition rotation does turn the label.\n\nThe frames are the same in a full paint and on the patched path a window uses, so this is how the renderer draws it, not a patching error. The shadow is a separate defect: it stays an axis-aligned rounded rectangle behind the turning box.\n\nCause, read from the code. The painter (renderer/paint/basic.rs and paint/motion.rs) pushes the binding's rotation onto the draw context's transform stack, which turns the primitives it emits. Text, SVGs and images are not emitted that way: `collect_render_elements_with_state` (blinc_app/src/context/element_collection.rs) places them, and it carries a CSS-transform affine down from `props.transform` (so CSS rotation turns text), the motion translate through the child offset, the motion scale about its centre, and the motion opacity, but never reads the binding's rotation (`get_motion_rotation` / `MotionBindings::get_rotation`, which only the painter, the layer replay and the CPU patcher read). The shadow shader (sdf_russl/shared/shadow.rs) reads neither a primitive's `rotation` nor its `local_affine`, so a shadow cannot turn under any rotation source; that one is probably the same for CSS rotation, not checked.\n\nThe GPU node table (122c606) has to decide what rotation does to glyphs and shadows, so this wants settling before it goes live. CSS turns both.","files":null}]}